## JUDGEMENT (from the tapped output, against the brief "tape saturation with a tilt EQ")
  1. Level: wet is +2.7 dB over bypass at the default Drive (A-B). Cause in the source: makeup is -drive/2 after a
     +drive push into tanh. A saturation stage should sit near unity at its default so the Mix/bypass comparison is
     honest. CHANGE: makeup = -drive (full compensation). Prediction: wet-dry broadband -> about -0.3 dB (tanh
     eats a little of the peaks), 8k/16k harmonics stay above dry.
  2. DC: the asymmetric curve tanh(x + 0.05x^2) rectifies a little; wet DC -68 dB vs dry -74 dB (6 dB added).
     Harmless for listening, but it is a measurable defect of the curve and it will pump a downstream compressor's
     detector. CHANGE: first-order high-pass at 5 Hz after the shelves. Prediction: wet DC returns to the dry floor.
  3. Tilt: as designed, no change.
