## VERDICT (#16)
  The loop closes from code: play -> tap -> spectrum -> judgement -> edit -> build (131 s) -> sign/validate/install
  (5 s) -> restart Logic (Save sheet answered, relaunch, alert, Open Recent: 51 s) -> re-measure (10 s).
  One iteration ~3.5 min of machine time, zero human steps (the 1.0.0 session's three human steps are all gone:
  pluginval de-quarantined, restart from code, plug-in window reopened by the project).
  How the agent judged the audio: Welch octave-band spectrum + DC + slope, A/B on the same 2 bars through the same
  tap; repeatability ~0.1 dB per band (A vs its accidental repeat), so differences > 0.5 dB are real. Not used:
  vision on a spectrogram, loudness models.
  Replacing an inserted plugin in a live session: SAFE (no crash, audio uninterrupted) but SILENT (D == A): Logic
  keeps executing the loaded image; the new code runs only after a Logic restart. A fresh insert in the same
  process was not tested (expected: same image, same old code — dyld does not reload a loaded bundle).
  Parameters for the A/B were set through the plug-in window's AX sliders (direct-child AXSlider, Int 0..10000)
  because the MCU plug-in edit page follows the Arrange-selected track and Stereo Out is not a track.
  Machine cost of a BUILD iteration on this laptop: version-bump rebuild 131 s (DSP-only edit ~76 s), restart 51 s.
